---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Emulation"
  description="Source acquisition and server-side JavaScript emulation model for December Reach."
>
  <header class="page-heading">
    <p class="page-context">Resources / Execution model</p>
    <h1>Emulation</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">The frontend obtains and prepares operating-system source. The JavaScript backend performs emulation. The browser provides access to the session.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="emulation-flow" aria-label="Emulation execution path">
    <article class="flow-stage">
      <span class="flow-index">01</span>
      <p class="flow-role">Frontend</p>
      <h2>Source acquisition</h2>
      <p>Acquire the operating-system source and preload what is needed before an emulation session begins.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="flow-stage">
      <span class="flow-index">02</span>
      <p class="flow-role">Backend</p>
      <h2>JavaScript emulation</h2>
      <p>The backend owns the emulation process and execution environment.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="flow-stage">
      <span class="flow-index">03</span>
      <p class="flow-role">Browser</p>
      <h2>Session access</h2>
      <p>The browser is the access surface. It is not the guest machine's execution host.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="responsibility-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Responsibility boundary</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="responsibility-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Frontend</h3>
        <p>Obtains and prepares the operating-system source for a session.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>JavaScript backend</h3>
        <p>Performs the emulation itself. CPU, memory and device behavior are not simulated by the website UI.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <aside class="document-note">The JavaScript emulation service is a separate execution component and is not bundled into the GitHub Pages frontend.</aside>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
